WEBVTT

00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:05,410
Okay, I'm going to show you how to add the headphone pad back on. It's very simple. Every once in a while

00:00:05,610 --> 00:00:06,610
It'll

00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:08,610
Slide off and if it gets caught on something

00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:15,770
But what you do is this black piece will just snap off. There are three little pegs

00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:19,370
You'll see you can just pull it up really easy

00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:22,510
Work your way around it

00:00:22,510 --> 00:00:24,510
And then I'll just pop off

00:00:24,510 --> 00:00:31,690
The nice thing is you have to worry about any wires or anything in there because this is you know by design a very simple

00:00:31,690 --> 00:00:35,710
product kind of cool to open it and actually see how it's just not much in there

00:00:35,710 --> 00:00:41,590
It's just designed to be the air tube sending the sound so there's no electronics right next to your head

00:00:42,190 --> 00:00:44,950
So what you do once that's off now this piece is loose

00:00:45,490 --> 00:00:48,530
It's held in place by the black piece when it's snapped on

00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:56,570
So don't worry about that being loose, but you just take the pad and you're just going to slide it over all the edges

00:00:57,250 --> 00:01:01,890
Very very simple to do it's a little stretchy so I usually do the bottom

00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:17,630
Side and then just kind of work your way around pull it over and there now it's back on and you'll see

00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:21,010
These are the three pegs that actually hold it on

00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:22,750
so

00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:25,710
Once that's done hold the red piece in place

00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:30,950
Actually that's a flip there. You can see the little notches or the

00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:34,150
Pigs go so just hold that

00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:39,990
Slide the air tube back through there to get it in its spot and then line it up with the pegs

00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:45,410
And then you simply just

00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:50,790
And you just snap it on and click some place and that's it

00:01:51,890 --> 00:01:53,890
Very very simple to fix very simple

00:01:54,690 --> 00:01:58,110
Basic product and not a lot of components to it and that's kind of how it's designed

